You are working on `autonomous-agent-nightshift`, a Claude Code skill + bash harness + npm CLI that runs AI agents overnight on user codebases.

CRITICAL CONVENTIONS:
- No emojis anywhere — code, docs, commits, comments. None.
- Bash 4+ compat. Shebang is `#!/usr/bin/env bash` (never `#!/bin/bash` — macOS bash 3.2).
- `set -euo pipefail` in every script. `shellcheck -S warning` must pass.
- Use `: > "$f"` for truncation, never `> "$f"` (SC2188).
- Cross-platform: prefer `perl -i -pe` over `sed -i ''` (BSD-only).
- No new dependencies in bash scripts. Only `claude`, `gh`, `git`, `bash` assumed.

PROJECT STRUCTURE:
- `SKILL.md` — Claude Code skill manifest. Triggers on phrases. Description 150-1000 chars with `NOT for:` clause.
- `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` — Plugin manifest with 6 slash commands.
- `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` — Marketplace manifest for `/plugin marketplace add`.
- `commands/nightshift-*.md` — Slash commands. Frontmatter `description:` only. Body = workflow.
- `scripts/` — Bash runners (run-agent-loop.sh, nightshift-bulletproof.sh, etc.)
- `bin/nightshift` — Unified CLI dispatcher.
- `docs/01-playbook.md` — Master 47KB guide. Canonical reference.
- `templates/` — Blank skeletons users copy into their projects.
- `examples/` — Reference artifacts (NEVER templates).
- `site/` — Vite + React landing page deployed to GitHub Pages.

VERSIONING:
- Semver. Patch = bugfix. Minor = new commands/features. Major = breaking.
- Tag as `vX.Y.Z`. CI auto-builds tarball on tag.
- CHANGELOG.md updated for every user-visible change.

WHEN MAKING CHANGES:
- Adding a slash command: also update plugin.json, install.sh hint list, bin/nightshift help, README table, CHANGELOG.
- Adding a doc: update README repo-layout, cross-link, increment numbering.
- Touching scripts: shellcheck pass, test idempotency, cross-platform sed.
- Updating SKILL.md description: keep 150-1000 chars, include NOT-for clause.

NEVER:
- Add tracking/telemetry/phone-home.
- Auto-commit changes the user's agent makes (classic runner never commits).
- Prompt inside the runner loop (it's detached overnight).
- Add emojis.
- Bundle API keys anywhere — `claude` CLI manages auth.

ALWAYS:
- Surface cost implications of features that call `claude -p` (it costs real money).
- Respect MAX_ITERATIONS as cost cap.
- Document why a release shipped (CHANGELOG "Why this release" section).
- Test on macOS and Linux paths (BSD sed != GNU sed).
- Read `docs/01-playbook.md` if you're unsure about behavior intent.

For full conventions see CLAUDE.md. For multi-agent coordination see AGENTS.md.
